      {
        "narration": "Thousands of ping pong balls vanished inside a Minnesota waterfall. At Devil\u2019s Kettle, half the river drops into a hole and disappears.",
        "visual_query": "devils kettle waterfall minnesota forest",
        "visual_fallback": "waterfall rock cavity"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Locals dropped dye, logs, and tracking gear down the throat. Nothing ever floated out into Lake Superior.",
        "visual_query": "brule river minnesota state park",
        "visual_fallback": "rushing river water"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Was the Earth drinking an entire river into deep subterranean caverns? The mystery stumped geologists for decades.",
        "visual_query": "minnesota north shore river gorge",
        "visual_fallback": "rocky canyon stream"
      },
      {
        "narration": "In 2017, hydrologists measured the river\u2019s water flow. The volume above and below the falls was identical.",
        "visual_query": "hydrologist water flow river measurement",
        "visual_fallback": "river flow measurement tool"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Immense water pressure inside the kettle crushes logs and balls into tiny pieces instantly. But if the exit is right there, how did every heavy object stay trapped inside?",
